From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dlls: restore XP menu animations and fades

Purpose: make XP popup menus and context menus open with their expected effects.
XP behavior: when menu animation and UI effects are enabled, MenuFade blends a
popup over 175 ms; otherwise XP reveals it from the direction in which it opens.
Wine before: win32u showed popup menus immediately, AnimateWindow was a partial
stub, X11 only exposed compositor opacity, and Wayland did not apply layered
window alpha or window regions to its surface.
Change: enable menu transitions and AnimateWindow's AW_BLEND and AW_SLIDE only
in the external XP shell. Without a compositor (WIN4WINE_COMPOSITED unset), a
fading menu stays opaque and shows the menu blended over a copy of the screen it
covers, flushing each frame as the menu thread reaches no message loop until the
end. X11 layered windows use _NET_WM_WINDOW_OPACITY, and an ordered-dither shape
when no compositor is present. Wayland applies constant alpha to
premultiplied pixels and uses an ARGB SHM surface to clip animated regions.
Each program reads UserPreferencesMask again when Display Properties' effects
change it (WM_SETTINGCHANGE with SPI_SETMENUANIMATION, SPI_SETMENUFADE and the
other user preference actions), so turning the menu effect off applies at once.
XP references:
  /home/gainsbarre/Projects/winxp_source/Source/XPSP1/NT/windows/core/ntuser/kernel/menu.c
  /home/gainsbarre/Projects/winxp_source/Source/XPSP1/NT/windows/core/ntuser/kernel/mnpopup.c
  /home/gainsbarre/Projects/winxp_source/Source/XPSP1/NT/shell/shell32/menuband/menubar.cpp
